// Criterion: an `rwfunc` return slot must also be a single type -- callers rely on it to type enclosing expressions.
//
// Negative case (4th state): layout is expected to fail, and the diagnostic must point to the return side.
// Kept separate from `types/rwfunc_union_parameter.kv` because parameter and return checks are two distinct
// branches in the implementation; a single combined test would miss an unguarded return branch.
//
// Reference: 03-type-system/05-langtype-signature-type-exprs.kv (normative section),
//            05-runtime-semantics/04-function-calls.kv.
// Expected error: rwfunc return type must be a single type

rwfunc pick(*int64 #x) -> (*int64|float64 #r) {
	0 -> *r
}
